<title>JAPAN: Japan July sorghum imports up 41.3 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan July sorghum imports up 41.3 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's sorghum imports in July totalled 177,394 tonnes, up by 41.3 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data showed on Wednesday. Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		     July 96	  June 96	 July 95</p>
<p> Total	     177,394	  146,892	 125,512</p>
<p>Major suppliers (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		 34,721	   41,815	  93,312</p>
<p> Australia	  68,754	   69,727	     nil</p>
<p> Argentina	  70,117	   33,350	  22,130</p>
<p> Sudan		   nil		nil	   9,001</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in the first seven months of 1996 were 1,157,091 tonnes against 1,125,863 tonnes in the year-ago period.</p>
</text>
